# tests/modifiers/xxmode.rxt — module `modifiers` (MOD-0.5c/d): the `xx`
# extended-mode hazard, the reason [MOD-0.5] was reordered after `classes`
# in the first place (docs/dev/plan_completed.md [MOD-0.5], D30 §7). R10/C2-11 measured:
# `[a- ]` at options=0 is error 108 (range out of order); `(?xx)[a- ]`
# COMPILES, because `xx` DELETES the space from the class body before
# range-parsing, at the exact class-range-endpoint spot `3fca0d8` (SPEC-FA)
# fixed as a silent-wrong-matcher one commit before the R-panel that found
# it. These are the cells that made pcrec's earlier safety an accident of
# `(?x)` being unimplemented rather than a designed guarantee — landing
# `xx` removes that accidental guard, so this file is the regression net
# for exactly the hazard the reordering was about.
#
# ORACLE: `# pcre2-only` throughout. Python has no `xx` distinct from `x` —
# `(?xx)a b` happens to behave like `(?x)a b` outside a class (both just
# see two 'x' letters in the flag group), but INSIDE a class python does
# NOT delete anything, so `(?xx)[a- ]` is a python compile ERROR ("bad
# character range a- ") where libpcre2/pcrec's xx COMPILES it — the two
# engines answer DIFFERENTLY on the discriminating cell, confirmed
# directly (scratchpad check against python3 `re` 2026-08-12) and recorded
# as docs/dev/upstream_issues.md U8. Every expectation below is measured
# against live libpcre2 10.46 instead (tests/probes/probe_mod05.c's
# "verdicts: x vs xx at the class boundary" and "matches: x/xx lexing"
# blocks, cross-checked with a throwaway scratchpad extension for the
# specific match spans used here).
#
# THE D33 §9.3 RECORD: run against the MOD-0.5a-gate binary via
#   PCREC=<binary> bash tests/harness/run.sh tests/modifiers/xxmode.rxt
# 11 cases total, 9 fail with "requires module 'modifiers'" (measured
# 2026-08-12) — the three `m`/`n` blocks (`(?xx)[a- ]`, `(?xx)[\ -a]`,
# `(?xx)[a\tb]`). The two `perr` blocks (`(?x)[a- ]`, `(?xx)[a-\ ]`)
# already PASS today: today's blanket gate refusal satisfies "fails to
# compile" just as well as the eventual err-108 diagnostic does.
# (Landing correction, same date: the tab block was split into escape-form
# and raw-byte-form — 14 cases now; see that block's own note.)

# ---- the D30 §7 hazard: single x leaves the range invalid ----------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?x)[a- ]
features modifiers
perr

# ---- xx DELETES the space first, so [a-] is left: members {a, -} ---------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)[a- ]
features modifiers
m "a" 0 1
m "-" 0 1
n " "

# ---- escaped space stays SIGNIFICANT even under xx: range a>SP invalid ---

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)[a-\ ]
features modifiers
perr

# ---- the mirrored range compiles: SP..a covers the low end -------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)[\ -a]
features modifiers
m " " 0 1
m "0" 0 1
m "a" 0 1

# ---- xx deletes RAW tab bytes; the \t ESCAPE survives ---------------------
# CORRECTED at the .5c/.5d landing (2026-08-12): this block originally
# expected `n "\t"` for the pattern spelled with backslash-t, transcribing
# the RAW-TAB measurement (probe_mod05.c) onto the ESCAPE form. The two are
# different constructs: xx deletes unescaped WHITESPACE BYTES {09,20};
# `\t` is an escape producing a tab MEMBER and is untouched by deletion.
# Measured both engines at the landing: libpcre2 10.46 MATCHES "\t" for
# the escape form, and pcrec agreed before the fix — the corpus was the
# wrong side of the disagreement. Both forms are pinned now; the raw-tab
# pattern line below embeds a literal 0x09 (pattern lines are verbatim).

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)[a\tb]
features modifiers
m "\t" 0 1
m "a" 0 1
m "b" 0 1

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)[a	b]
features modifiers
n "\t"
m "a" 0 1
m "b" 0 1

# ---- R17 additions (checks critic, 2026-08-12): the x-LEVEL rules --------
# The level is assigned per occurrence by ADJACENCY (probe_mod05c.c):
# (?xsx) is level 1 — an implementation that COUNTS x occurrences reads it
# as xx and deletes the class-interior space. These are the only make-test
# pins of the adjacency rule and the cross-run downgrade.

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xsx)[a b]
features modifiers
m " " 0 1
m "a" 0 1

# a later bare (?x) DOWNGRADES an earlier (?xx) (the (?xx)(?s) control in
# probe_mod05c.c keeps deletion; this cell is the downgrade direction).
# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)(?x)[a b]
features modifiers
m " " 0 1
